# Refactor-before-features policy

Until epic [#131](https://github.com/FioraSolutions/Fineage/issues/131) P0 items are complete, **architecture refactoring takes priority over new features**.

## Active policy

1. **Pause `smoke:gremlin`** (epic [#129](https://github.com/FioraSolutions/Fineage/issues/129)) — content delivery is blocked pending CI + refactor base.
2. **Do not add new members** to `IncomingPacketActions.cs` — surface is frozen per [#137](https://github.com/FioraSolutions/Fineage/issues/137).
3. **Do not expand `GameManager`** responsibilities. Extract to focused classes per [#141](https://github.com/FioraSolutions/Fineage/issues/141).
4. **New networking code** must go through `IZoneTransport` interface, not inline `IsZoneV2` checks.
5. **New code must be testable** — prefer constructor/method injection over `static Instance` singletons.

## Worktree protocol

- Each branch gets its own worktree. Never reuse another agent's branch.
- Do not push directly to `main` or `dev`. Land via PR into `dev`.
- See `Docs/AGENT_BRANCH_PROTOCOL.md` for full rules.

## Priority order (from CLIENT_ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW.md)

1. [#137](https://github.com/FioraSolutions/Fineage/issues/137) — Freeze IncomingPacketActions surface
2. [#139](https://github.com/FioraSolutions/Fineage/issues/139) — Assembly definition split
3. [#140](https://github.com/FioraSolutions/Fineage/issues/140) — Wire V2 through IZoneTransport
4. [#141](https://github.com/FioraSolutions/Fineage/issues/141) — Decompose GameManager
5. [#142](https://github.com/FioraSolutions/Fineage/issues/142) — Migrate IncomingPacketActions to DI
